    def all_product_availability(
        self,
        project_id: str,
        *,
        name: str | None | NotGiven = NOT_GIVEN,
        name_contains: str | None | NotGiven = NOT_GIVEN,
        region: str | None | NotGiven = NOT_GIVEN,
        type: models.PublicCloudReferenceProductTypeEnum | str | None | NotGiven = NOT_GIVEN,
    ) -> t.AsyncIterator[models.PublicCloudReferenceProductAvailability]:
        """all_product_availability iterates over GET /v2/publicCloud/project/{projectId}/reference/productAvailability (Get product availability).

        It yields one item at a time, and gets the next page only when the loop reaches it.
        An error is raised and stops the loop. Use it with ``async for``.

        Product availability

        Returns the products available to this Public Cloud project, grouped by product type.

        This is read-only reference data: the response is computed from the OVHcloud commercial
        catalog combined with the project's entitlements and its quota usage. It does not reflect
        existing resources and triggers no OpenStack call.

        The response is an array with one entry per product type, in this order: `INSTANCE`,
        `VOLUME`, `LOADBALANCER`, `GATEWAY`, `FLOATING_IP`, `PUBLIC_IP`, `VOLUME_SNAPSHOT`,
        `VOLUME_BACKUP`, `INSTANCE_SNAPSHOT`, `SHARE`, `SHARE_SNAPSHOT`, `OBJECT_STORAGE`, `SWIFT`.
        Each type group carries its `models`. Each model carries the `locations` where it is sold to
        the project, in the regions activated on the project and in those the project can activate.
        Each location reports its availability zones, `regionActivated`, a `quotaStatus` with the
        quota resources that block it (`quotaLimitedBy`) and, for the `INSTANCE` type only, a
        `stockStatus` per availability zone.

        `links` point to related operations: a `SPECS` link on a model leads to the reference route
        describing it, and a location whose `quotaStatus` is `INSUFFICIENT` carries a `QUOTA` link.

        Every filter is optional: `type` keeps the group of that product type only, `region` the
        locations of that region (letter case ignored), `name` the models with exactly that name and
        `nameContains` the models whose name contains that value (letter case ignored).

        Args:
            project_id: Project ID
            name: Optional exact model name filter, for example b3-8 (optional)
            name_contains: Optional model name filter keeping the names that contain this value, letter case ignored (optional)
            region: Optional region filter, letter case ignored (optional)
            type: Optional product type filter (optional)

        Requires the IAM action publicCloudProject:apiovh:reference/productAvailability/get.
        """
        return self._pages(
            _r.OP_ALL_PRODUCT_AVAILABILITY,
            path_params={
                "projectId": project_id,
            },
            query=(
                ("name", name),
                ("nameContains", name_contains),
                ("region", region),
                ("type", type),
            ),
            item=models.PublicCloudReferenceProductAvailability,
        )

